From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiny <owner@shinychang.net>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:11:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let Talk to Shy drive tabs, read the network and show
 its progress

- Agents get tools through chrome.debugger: screenshot, run_script,
  click, type_text, press_key, scroll, navigate, and the network log
  (network_requests, network_request) with credentials hidden. The
  debugger infobar stays away for Talk to Shy, whose panel lists every
  call.
- "Use and drive any site without asking" is on by default. Turned off,
  each site and each kind of action waits for the user to allow it.
- The composer takes files from the + button, paste or drop.
- While the agent works, a line under the chat says what it is doing,
  and the tools a reply used fold up under it instead of sitting in
  the text.
- Shift+Cmd+S opens and closes the panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYkQJUafT3hpFT1kBmDgzX
